01,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan scope-out: 'Legacy module-level entry points invoked without a call_timeout (no composed runtime) keep the ambient _acli_call_timeout() resolve — that is the compatibility floor'","backend.py:422 `transport = acli.AcliClient(jira_url=s.url, user=s.user, api_token=s.api_token, jira_project=s.project)` — the @register(\\\"jira\\\") factory, distinct from runtime._build_cloud which the plan DOES wire","The composed runtime path uses _build_cloud (runtime.py:145), not this registry factory, so leaving it on the ambient floor is defensible — but the scope-out wording ('module-level entry points') does not obviously cover a registered factory function"],"finding":"The scope-out for legacy ambient-timeout paths names 'legacy module-level entry points' but the registered `@register(\"jira\")` backend factory `_build_jira_backend` (adapters/jira/backend.py:422) also constructs `AcliClient(...)` without a `call_timeout`, and it is a factory function rather than a bare module-level entry point — leaving it ambiguous whether that construction is intentionally left on the ambient `_acli_call_timeout()` floor.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd9fb9adba41168de","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Explicit scope-outs' paragraph; src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/backend.py:422","norm_id":"n8035c369a8f58864","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer reviewing bypass sites finds the backend.py:422 AcliClient construction and is unsure whether to thread a timeout there or leave it ambient"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily